      "body": "## Summary\n\n`MonetrixAccountant` treats HyperCore 0x811 Borrow-Lend state as supply-only. It counts `supply.value` as protocol backing, but it never reads or subtracts `borrow.value`.\n\nHyperCore 0x811 is not a supply-only state. The public Hyperliquid EVM precompile library models the user token state as `BorrowLendUserTokenState`, containing both `borrow` and `supply`, each with `basis` and `value`. The Hyperliquid Portfolio Margin documentation also describes borrowed assets as real liabilities that accrue interest and are borrowed against eligible collateral. See [`PrecompileLib.sol`](https://github.com/hyperliquid-dev/hyper-evm-lib/blob/main/src/PrecompileLib.sol) and [`Portfolio margin`](https://hyperliquid.gitbook.io/hyperliquid-docs/trading/portfolio-margin).\n\nBecause Monetrix only accounts the positive supply side, a Borrow-Lend liability can be omitted from backing. This inflates `totalBackingSigned()`, makes `surplus()` and `distributableSurplus()` artificially positive, and allows `MonetrixVault.settle()` to move real USDC into `YieldEscrow` as yield even when the correct net surplus is zero.\n\n##\n\n### Severity: **Medium**\n\n##\n\n## Impact\n\nThe impact is material surplus overstatement and unbacked yield settlement.\n\nIf the Vault has this 0x811 state:\n\n```text\nsupplied collateral value = 100,000 USDC\nborrow liability          = 100,000 USDC\n```\n\nThe correct net Borrow-Lend value is:\n\n```text\n100,000 - 100,000 = 0\n```\n\nThe current Accountant reports:\n\n```text\n100,000\n```\n\nbecause it counts only `supply.value`.\n\nThat phantom surplus can pass the `settleDailyPnL()` distributable-surplus gate and cause the Vault to transfer real USDC to `YieldEscrow`. This is not only an incorrect view. The proof of concept shows `settle(100e6)` succeeds, `YieldEscrow` receives `100e6` USDC, and the correct net surplus becomes negative afterward.\n\nThis is Medium severity because it breaks core backing and yield-settlement invariants. It is not High because the path is not a direct permissionless drain, the settlement path is still bounded by the yield pipeline, and the issue depends on a Borrow-Lend liability existing in the Vault's Portfolio Margin state.\n\n---\n\n## Why this is not an Operator trust assumption\n\nThis issue does not rely on a compromised Operator.\n\nThe Operator only uses normal protocol functions:\n\n* `supplyToBlp()` to register supplied slots through the intended BLP path\n* `settle()` to run the intended yield settlement path\n\nThe bug is in the Accountant's interpretation of the 0x811 state. Once the protocol uses Borrow-Lend supply values as backing, it must also account for Borrow-Lend liabilities. The contracts do not enforce `borrow.value == 0`, do not subtract `borrow.value`, and do not prove the liability is netted elsewhere before settling yield.\n\nThe Accountant is the on-chain gate that should prevent phantom surplus from being settled. The Operator submits an amount that the on-chain gate accepts. The failure is that the gate is computed from gross supply accounting instead of net Borrow-Lend accounting.\n\nSo the issue is not:\n\n* Operator theft\n* Governor compromise\n* Upgrader compromise\n* emergency function abuse\n* multisig backing abuse\n* sUSDM virtual share behavior\n* the previously reported `_sendL1Bridge` held-balance issue\n\nThe issue is incomplete net accounting of a backing source.\n\n---\n\n## Why the Borrow-Lend liability must reduce backing\n\nThe 0x811 state includes both sides of the Borrow-Lend position:\n\n```solidity\nstruct BasisAndValue {\n    uint64 basis;\n    uint64 value;\n}\n\nstruct BorrowLendUserTokenState {\n    BasisAndValue borrow;\n    BasisAndValue supply;\n}\n```\n\nThat state exposes an asset side and a liability side. Treating the returned state as supply-only is economically incorrect. See [`PrecompileLib.sol`](https://github.com/hyperliquid-dev/hyper-evm-lib/blob/main/src/PrecompileLib.sol).\n\nThe Portfolio Margin documentation states that insufficient balances can be borrowed against eligible collateral, and that borrowed assets accrue interest. That means the borrow side is a real liability, not harmless metadata. See [`Portfolio margin`](https://hyperliquid.gitbook.io/hyperliquid-docs/trading/portfolio-margin).\n\nThe account abstraction documentation also states that for unified account and portfolio margin, balances and holds appear in the spot clearinghouse state and individual perp DEX user states are not meaningful. That makes it unsafe for Monetrix to assume that a Borrow-Lend liability is always netted somewhere else in `accountValueSigned()`. See [`Account abstraction modes`](https://hyperliquid.gitbook.io/hyperliquid-docs/trading/account-abstraction-modes).\n\n---\n\n## Vulnerability details\n\n### 1. `suppliedBalance()` decodes the 0x811 response but returns only the fourth field\n\nFrom [`PrecompileReader.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/PrecompileReader.sol#L84-L91):\n\n```solidity\nfunction suppliedBalance(address account, uint64 token) internal view returns (uint64 supplied) {\n    (bool ok, bytes memory res) = HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE.staticcall(\n        abi.encode(account, token)\n    );\n    require(ok && res.length >= 128, \"PrecompileReader: supplied balance read failed\");\n    (,,, supplied) = abi.decode(res, (uint64, uint64, uint64, uint64));\n}\n```\n\nThe decoded response contains four `uint64` values. Under the 0x811 Borrow-Lend layout, these correspond to:\n\n```text\nborrow.basis\nborrow.value\nsupply.basis\nsupply.value\n```\n\nThe code discards the first three fields and returns only the fourth field, `supply.value`.\n\nThis means `borrow.value` is ignored at the first accounting boundary.\n\n---\n\n### 2. USDC supplied value is converted to EVM units, but USDC borrow value is never read\n\nFrom [`PrecompileReader.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/PrecompileReader.sol#L132-L136):\n\n```solidity\nfunction suppliedUsdcEvm(address account) internal view returns (uint256) {\n    uint64 supplied = suppliedBalance(account, uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX));\n    return TokenMath.usdcL1WeiToEvm(supplied);\n}\n```\n\nThis helper converts only the returned `supplied` value into 6-decimal EVM USDC units. There is no matching helper for `borrow.value`, and there is no netting step.\n\nAs a result, a USDC Borrow-Lend liability can be present in 0x811 while contributing nothing negative to backing.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Non-USDC supplied collateral is valued as USDC notional, but non-USDC borrow liabilities are also ignored\n\nFrom [`PrecompileReader.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/PrecompileReader.sol#L151-L162):\n\n```solidity\nfunction suppliedNotionalUsdcFromPerp(\n    uint32 spotTokenIndex,\n    uint32 perpIndex,\n    address account\n) internal view returns (uint256) {\n    uint64 supplied = suppliedBalance(account, uint64(spotTokenIndex));\n    if (supplied == 0) return 0;\n    uint64 price = oraclePx(perpIndex);\n    (uint8 weiDec, uint8 szDec) = _assetDecimals(spotTokenIndex, perpIndex);\n    return TokenMath.spotNotionalUsdcFromPerpPx(supplied, price, weiDec, szDec);\n}\n```\n\nFor non-USDC assets, the code values `supply.value` through the oracle and decimal path, then counts that amount as USDC backing. Again, the borrow side of the same Borrow-Lend state is not read or subtracted.\n\nThe proof of concept uses this stronger cross-token shape:\n\n```text\nnon-USDC supplied collateral = 100,000 USDC notional\nUSDC borrow liability        = 100,000 USDC\ncorrect net 0x811 value      = 0\nreported 0x811 backing       = 100,000 USDC\n```\n\nThis avoids relying on a same-token supply and borrow state.\n\n---\n\n### 4. The notional conversion is correct, but it is applied only to the supply side\n\nFrom [`TokenMath.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/TokenMath.sol#L56-L69):\n\n```solidity\nfunction spotNotionalUsdcFromPerpPx(\n    uint64 balWei,\n    uint64 rawPerpOraclePx,\n    uint8 weiDecimals,\n    uint8 perpSzDecimals\n) internal pure returns (uint256) {\n    if (balWei == 0 || rawPerpOraclePx == 0) return 0;\n    require(weiDecimals >= perpSzDecimals, \"TokenMath: invalid decimals\");\n    uint256 divisor = 10 ** uint256(weiDecimals - perpSzDecimals);\n    return (uint256(balWei) * uint256(rawPerpOraclePx)) / divisor;\n}\n```\n\nThe proof of concept uses the real conversion path:\n\n```text\nASSET_BAL_WEI = 10,000,000,000\nASSET_RAW_PX  = 10,000\nweiDecimals   = 8\nperpSzDecimals = 5\n\nnotional = 10,000,000,000 * 10,000 / 10^(8 - 5)\n         = 100,000,000,000\n         = 100,000e6 USDC\n```\n\nThe issue is not the decimal math. The issue is that the converted value is added for supplied collateral while the matching Borrow-Lend liability is omitted.\n\n---\n\n### 5. `totalBackingSigned()` uses `_readL1Backing()` as part of protocol backing\n\nFrom [`MonetrixAccountant.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol#L117-L134):\n\n```solidity\nfunction totalBackingSigned() public view returns (int256 total) {\n    total = int256(usdc.balanceOf(vault));\n    address re = IMonetrixVaultReader(vault).redeemEscrow();\n    if (re != address(0)) {\n        total += int256(usdc.balanceOf(re));\n    }\n\n    total += _readL1Backing(vault, vaultSupplied);\n    address _multisigVault = IMonetrixVaultReader(vault).multisigVault();\n    if (_multisigVault != address(0)) {\n        total += _readL1Backing(_multisigVault, multisigSupplied);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe output of `_readL1Backing()` directly affects the signed backing value used by the rest of the accounting system.\n\n---\n\n### 6. `_readL1Backing()` adds supplied values but never subtracts Borrow-Lend liabilities\n\nFrom [`MonetrixAccountant.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol#L137-L172):\n\n```solidity\nfunction _readL1Backing(address account, SuppliedAsset[] storage suppliedList)\n    internal view returns (int256 total)\n{\n    total = _readPerpAccountValueSigned(account);\n    total += int256(_readSpotUsdcBalance(account));\n\n    uint256 slen = suppliedList.length;\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < slen; i++) {\n        SuppliedAsset storage a = suppliedList[i];\n        if (a.spotToken == uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)) {\n            total += int256(PrecompileReader.suppliedUsdcEvm(account));\n        } else {\n            total += int256(\n                PrecompileReader.suppliedNotionalUsdcFromPerp(uint32(a.spotToken), a.perpIndex, account)\n            );\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (config != address(0)) {\n        IMonetrixConfigReader cfg = IMonetrixConfigReader(config);\n        uint256 len = cfg.tradeableAssetsLength();\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n            (uint32 perpIndex, uint32 spotIndex, ) = cfg.tradeableAssets(i);\n            total += int256(_readSpotAssetUsdc(spotIndex, perpIndex, account));\n        }\n    }\n\n    total += int256(_readHlpEquity(account));\n}\n```\n\nThe 0x811 loop only adds supplied values. It never reads `borrow.value` and never applies a negative adjustment for liabilities.\n\nThis causes `totalBackingSigned()` to be overstated whenever the Vault has a Borrow-Lend liability.\n\n---\n\n### 7. `supplyToBlp()` registers supplied slots through the real Vault path\n\nFrom [`MonetrixVault.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixVault.sol#L333-L346):\n\n```solidity\nfunction supplyToBlp(uint64 token, uint64 l1Amount) external onlyOperator whenOperatorNotPaused {\n    require(l1Amount > 0, \"zero amount\");\n    ActionEncoder.sendSupply(token, l1Amount);\n    if (accountant != address(0)) {\n        uint32 perpIndex = 0;\n        if (token != uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)) {\n            require(config.isSpotWhitelisted(uint32(token)), \"spot not whitelisted\");\n            perpIndex = config.spotToPerp(uint32(token));\n        }\n        MonetrixAccountant(accountant).notifyVaultSupply(token, perpIndex);\n    }\n    emit BlpSupplied(token, l1Amount);\n}\n```\n\nThe proof of concept uses this real path to register both the non-USDC supplied slot and the USDC liability slot. The bug is not caused by manually writing to the Accountant registry.\n\n---\n\n### 8. The inflated backing directly feeds `surplus()` and `distributableSurplus()`\n\nFrom [`MonetrixAccountant.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol#L180-L191):\n\n```solidity\nfunction surplus() public view returns (int256) {\n    return totalBackingSigned() - int256(usdm.totalSupply());\n}\n\nfunction distributableSurplus() public view returns (int256) {\n    int256 s = surplus();\n    address re = IMonetrixVaultReader(vault).redeemEscrow();\n    uint256 sf = re == address(0) ? 0 : IRedeemEscrow(re).shortfall();\n    return s - int256(sf);\n}\n```\n\nIf `totalBackingSigned()` is inflated by ignored debt, `surplus()` and `distributableSurplus()` are inflated by the same amount.\n\n---\n\n### 9. `settleDailyPnL()` accepts yield against the inflated `distributableSurplus()`\n\nFrom [`MonetrixAccountant.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol#L200-L227):\n\n```solidity\nfunction settleDailyPnL(uint256 proposedYield)\n    external\n    onlyVault\n    returns (uint256 distributable)\n{\n    require(lastSettlementTime > 0, \"Accountant: not initialized\");\n    require(\n        block.timestamp >= lastSettlementTime + minSettlementInterval,\n        \"Accountant: settlement too early\"\n    );\n    int256 ds = distributableSurplus();\n    require(ds > 0, \"Accountant: no distributable surplus\");\n    distributable = uint256(ds);\n    require(proposedYield <= distributable, \"Accountant: exceeds distributable\");\n\n    uint256 elapsed = block.timestamp - lastSettlementTime;\n    uint256 cap = (usdm.totalSupply() * IMonetrixConfigReader(config).maxAnnualYieldBps() * elapsed)\n        / (10_000 * 365 days);\n    require(proposedYield <= cap, \"Accountant: exceeds annualized cap\");\n\n    lastSettlementTime = block.timestamp;\n    totalSettledYield += proposedYield;\n}\n```\n\nGate 3 is intended to prevent settlement above real distributable surplus. Because Borrow-Lend liabilities are omitted, this gate can approve yield that does not exist under net backing.\n\n---\n\n### 10. `settle()` then moves real USDC into `YieldEscrow`\n\nFrom [`MonetrixVault.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixVault.sol#L364-L375):\n\n```solidity\nfunction settle(uint256 proposedYield) external onlyOperator requireWired nonReentrant whenNotPaused whenOperatorNotPaused {\n    require(proposedYield > 0, \"zero yield\");\n\n    uint256 vaultBal = usdc.balanceOf(address(this));\n    uint256 shortfall_ = IRedeemEscrow(redeemEscrow).shortfall();\n    uint256 available = vaultBal > shortfall_ ? vaultBal - shortfall_ : 0;\n    require(available >= proposedYield, \"insufficient EVM USDC\");\n\n    IMonetrixAccountant(accountant).settleDailyPnL(proposedYield);\n    usdc.safeTransfer(yieldEscrow, proposedYield);\n    emit YieldCollected(proposedYield);\n}\n```\n\nThis converts the accounting error into a real asset movement. USDC leaves the Vault and enters `YieldEscrow` as yield even though net backing has no surplus.\n\n---",
      "proofOfConcept": "## Attack scenario\n\nA realistic sequence is:\n\n1. Users deposit `1,000,000e6` USDC and receive `1,000,000e6` USDM.\n2. The Vault has `1,000,000e6` EVM USDC backing.\n3. A non-USDC PM or BLP supplied slot has `100,000e6` USDC of notional value.\n4. The Vault also has a `100,000e6` USDC Borrow-Lend liability in the 0x811 state.\n5. The correct net Borrow-Lend value is zero.\n6. The Accountant reports `100,000e6` of surplus because it counts only `supply.value`.\n7. After the settlement interval passes, the Operator calls `settle(100e6)`.\n8. `settleDailyPnL()` accepts the proposed yield because `distributableSurplus()` is inflated.\n9. The Vault transfers `100e6` real USDC to `YieldEscrow`.\n10. Correct net surplus becomes negative by `100e6`.\n\nThis is not caused by a malicious Operator. It is caused by the Accountant treating a Borrow-Lend state as supply-only.\n\n---\n\n## Proof of Concept\n\nThe Solidity proof of concept demonstrates the issue using the real `MonetrixVault.settle()` and `MonetrixAccountant` accounting paths.\n\n### What the proof of concept proves\n\n1. The Vault starts with `1,000,000e6` EVM USDC and `1,000,000e6` USDM supply.\n2. A cross-token PM or BLP supplied asset is registered through the real `supplyToBlp()` path.\n3. The supplied asset is worth `100,000e6` USDC under the real `TokenMath.spotNotionalUsdcFromPerpPx()` conversion.\n4. The 0x811 precompile mock returns a valid Borrow-Lend layout with non-USDC `supply.value` and USDC `borrow.value`.\n5. The A/B check proves that changing `borrow.value` from zero to `100,000e6` does not change reported backing or reported surplus.\n6. The Accountant reports `100,000e6` surplus while the correct net surplus is zero.\n7. `settle(100e6)` succeeds.\n8. `YieldEscrow` receives `100e6` real USDC.\n9. Correct net surplus becomes `-100e6` after settlement.\n10. The test does not use multisig backing, emergency functions, upgrades, sUSDM virtual shares, or the held-spot bridge-back bug.\n\nThe executed output confirms the key economic facts: reported surplus remains `100000000000` before settlement, correct net surplus is `0`, borrow liability has zero effect on reported surplus, `YieldEscrow` receives `100000000`, and correct surplus after settlement is `-100000000`.\n\n### Install prerequisites\n\n```bash\nsudo apt update\nsudo apt install -y git build-essential curl clang pkg-config libssl-dev cmake\n```\n\n### Install Foundry\n\n```bash\ncurl -L https://foundry.paradigm.xyz | bash\nsource ~/.bashrc\nfoundryup\n```\n\n### Clone the repository\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix.git\ncd 2026-04-monetrix\ngit checkout 3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e\ngit submodule update --init --recursive\n```\n\n### Install project dependencies\n\n```bash\nnvm install 18\nnvm use 18\nexport HUSKY=0\nyarn install\n```\n\n### Modify the `test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol` file\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p test/c4\nnano test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol\n```\n\n```solidity\n// File: test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\n\nimport {USDM} from \"../../src/tokens/USDM.sol\";\nimport {sUSDM} from \"../../src/tokens/sUSDM.sol\";\nimport {sUSDMEscrow} from \"../../src/tokens/sUSDMEscrow.sol\";\n\nimport {InsuranceFund} from \"../../src/core/InsuranceFund.sol\";\nimport {MonetrixAccountant} from \"../../src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol\";\nimport {MonetrixConfig} from \"../../src/core/MonetrixConfig.sol\";\nimport {MonetrixVault} from \"../../src/core/MonetrixVault.sol\";\nimport {PrecompileReader} from \"../../src/core/PrecompileReader.sol\";\nimport {RedeemEscrow} from \"../../src/core/RedeemEscrow.sol\";\nimport {TokenMath} from \"../../src/core/TokenMath.sol\";\nimport {YieldEscrow} from \"../../src/core/YieldEscrow.sol\";\n\nimport {MonetrixAccessController} from \"../../src/governance/MonetrixAccessController.sol\";\nimport {HyperCoreConstants} from \"../../src/interfaces/HyperCoreConstants.sol\";\n\nimport {MockUSDC} from \"../mocks/MockUSDC.sol\";\nimport {MockCoreDepositWallet} from \"../mocks/MockCoreDepositWallet.sol\";\n\ncontract _PoCMockCoreWriter {\n    event ActionSent(bytes action);\n\n    function sendRawAction(bytes calldata action) external {\n        emit ActionSent(action);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract _PoCMockPrecompile {\n    mapping(bytes32 => bytes) public responses;\n\n    function setResponse(bytes calldata callData, bytes calldata response) external {\n        responses[keccak256(callData)] = response;\n    }\n\n    fallback(bytes calldata data) external payable returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes memory r = responses[keccak256(data)];\n        if (r.length == 0) return new bytes(128);\n        return r;\n    }\n}\n\n/*\n============================================================================================================================================\nSOURCES\n=======\n\n* src/core/PrecompileReader.sol:84-91\n* src/core/PrecompileReader.sol:132-136\n* src/core/PrecompileReader.sol:151-162\n* src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol:117-134\n* src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol:137-172\n* src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol:180-191\n* src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol:200-227\n* src/core/MonetrixVault.sol:333-346\n* src/core/MonetrixVault.sol:364-375\n* src/core/ActionEncoder.sol:138-147\n* src/core/TokenMath.sol:18-25\n* src/core/TokenMath.sol:56-69\n* src/interfaces/HyperCoreConstants.sol:11-33\n* test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol\n\n============================================================================================================================================\nBORROW-LEND LIABILITY BACKING MISACCOUNT\n0X811 SUPPLY.VALUE IS COUNTED AS BACKING WHILE BORROW.VALUE IS IGNORED\n============================================================================================================================================\n\nThis PoC demonstrates that MonetrixAccountant accounts the supply.value side of\nHyperCore 0x811 Borrow-Lend state as backing, but never subtracts borrow.value.\n\nThe test uses a cross-token PM/BLP state:\n    * non-USDC supplied collateral has 100,000 USDC of notional value\n    * USDC borrow liability is 100,000 USDC\n    * correct net 0x811 value is therefore zero\n\nThe current Accountant reports 100,000 USDC of surplus anyway and allows\nMonetrixVault.settle(100e6) to move real USDC into YieldEscrow.\n*/\n\ncontract C4Submission is Test {\n    MonetrixAccessController public acl;\n    USDM public usdm;\n    sUSDM public susdm;\n    sUSDMEscrow public unstakeEscrow;\n    InsuranceFund public insurance;\n    MonetrixConfig public config;\n    MonetrixVault public vault;\n    MonetrixAccountant public accountant;\n    RedeemEscrow public redeemEscrow;\n    YieldEscrow public yieldEscrow;\n\n    MockUSDC public usdc;\n    MockCoreDepositWallet public depositWallet;\n\n    address public admin = address(0xAD);\n    address public operator = address(0xBB);\n    address public foundation = address(0xF0);\n    address public user1 = address(0x1);\n    address public user2 = address(0x2);\n\n    uint256 internal constant DEPOSIT_EVM = 1_000_000e6;\n    uint256 internal constant SUPPLIED_USDC = 100_000e6;\n    uint256 internal constant BORROW_USDC = 100_000e6;\n    uint256 internal constant YIELD = 100e6;\n\n    uint32 internal constant ASSET_SPOT = 150;\n    uint32 internal constant ASSET_PERP = 159;\n    uint32 internal constant ASSET_PAIR = 10107;\n    uint8 internal constant ASSET_WEI_DEC = 8;\n    uint8 internal constant ASSET_SZ_DEC = 5;\n    uint64 internal constant ASSET_BAL = 10_000_000_000;\n    uint64 internal constant ASSET_PX = 10_000;\n\n    int256 internal abBackingNoDebt;\n    int256 internal abBackingWithDebt;\n    int256 internal abSurplusNoDebt;\n    int256 internal abSurplusWithDebt;\n\n    function setUp() public virtual {\n        usdc = new MockUSDC();\n        depositWallet = new MockCoreDepositWallet(address(usdc));\n\n        vm.startPrank(admin);\n\n        acl = MonetrixAccessController(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(new MonetrixAccessController()),\n                    abi.encodeCall(MonetrixAccessController.initialize, (admin))\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        usdm = USDM(\n            address(new ERC1967Proxy(address(new USDM()), abi.encodeCall(USDM.initialize, (address(acl)))))\n        );\n\n        insurance = InsuranceFund(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(new InsuranceFund()),\n                    abi.encodeCall(InsuranceFund.initialize, (address(usdc), address(acl)))\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        config = MonetrixConfig(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(new MonetrixConfig()),\n                    abi.encodeCall(MonetrixConfig.initialize, (address(insurance), foundation, address(acl)))\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        susdm = sUSDM(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(new sUSDM()),\n                    abi.encodeCall(sUSDM.initialize, (address(usdm), address(config), address(acl)))\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        vault = MonetrixVault(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(new MonetrixVault()),\n                    abi.encodeCall(\n                        MonetrixVault.initialize,\n                        (\n                            address(usdc),\n                            address(usdm),\n                            address(susdm),\n                            address(config),\n                            address(depositWallet),\n                            address(acl)\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        accountant = MonetrixAccountant(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(new MonetrixAccountant()),\n                    abi.encodeCall(\n                        MonetrixAccountant.initialize,\n                        (address(vault), address(usdc), address(usdm), address(acl))\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        redeemEscrow = RedeemEscrow(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(new RedeemEscrow()),\n                    abi.encodeCall(RedeemEscrow.initialize, (address(usdc), address(vault), address(acl)))\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        yieldEscrow = YieldEscrow(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(new YieldEscrow()),\n                    abi.encodeCall(YieldEscrow.initialize, (address(usdc), address(vault), address(acl)))\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        acl.grantRole(acl.GOVERNOR(), admin);\n        acl.grantRole(acl.GUARDIAN(), admin);\n        acl.grantRole(acl.OPERATOR(), admin);\n        acl.grantRole(acl.OPERATOR(), operator);\n        acl.grantRole(acl.UPGRADER(), admin);\n\n        usdm.setVault(address(vault));\n        susdm.setVault(address(vault));\n\n        unstakeEscrow = new sUSDMEscrow(address(usdm), address(susdm));\n        susdm.setEscrow(address(unstakeEscrow));\n\n        vault.setAccountant(address(accountant));\n        vault.setRedeemEscrow(address(redeemEscrow));\n        vault.setYieldEscrow(address(yieldEscrow));\n        accountant.setConfig(address(config));\n        accountant.initializeSettlement();\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_ACCOUNT_MARGIN_SUMMARY, address(new _PoCMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SPOT_BALANCE, address(new _PoCMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_ORACLE_PX, address(new _PoCMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_VAULT_EQUITY, address(new _PoCMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE, address(new _PoCMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_PERP_ASSET_INFO, address(new _PoCMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_TOKEN_INFO, address(new _PoCMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_POSITION, address(new _PoCMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SPOT_PX, address(new _PoCMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.CORE_WRITER, address(new _PoCMockCoreWriter()).code);\n\n        usdc.mint(user1, 1_000_000e6);\n        usdc.mint(user2, 1_000_000e6);\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() public {\n        uint64 borrowL1 = TokenMath.usdcEvmToL1Wei(BORROW_USDC);\n        uint256 suppliedComputed = TokenMath.spotNotionalUsdcFromPerpPx(\n            ASSET_BAL,\n            ASSET_PX,\n            ASSET_WEI_DEC,\n            ASSET_SZ_DEC\n        );\n\n        assertEq(suppliedComputed, SUPPLIED_USDC, \"supplied notional\");\n\n        seed(DEPOSIT_EVM);\n        openBlp();\n        mockAsset();\n\n        mockBlp(uint64(ASSET_SPOT), 0, ASSET_BAL);\n\n        // A/B proof. First, report surplus with no USDC borrow liability.\n        mockBlp(uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX), 0, 0);\n        abBackingNoDebt = accountant.totalBackingSigned();\n        abSurplusNoDebt = accountant.surplus();\n\n        // Then set a 100,000 USDC borrow liability while leaving supply.value at zero.\n        // The reported backing and surplus do not change, proving borrow.value is ignored.\n        mockBlp(uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX), borrowL1, 0);\n        abBackingWithDebt = accountant.totalBackingSigned();\n        abSurplusWithDebt = accountant.surplus();\n\n        assertEq(abBackingWithDebt, abBackingNoDebt, \"borrow.value ignored by reported backing\");\n        assertEq(abSurplusWithDebt, abSurplusNoDebt, \"borrow.value ignored by reported surplus\");\n        assertEq(abSurplusNoDebt, int256(SUPPLIED_USDC), \"no-debt reported surplus\");\n        assertEq(abSurplusWithDebt, int256(SUPPLIED_USDC), \"debt reported surplus still counts supply only\");\n\n        assertEq(usdm.totalSupply(), DEPOSIT_EVM, \"USDM supply\");\n        assertEq(usdc.balanceOf(address(vault)), DEPOSIT_EVM, \"vault USDC\");\n        assertEq(accountant.vaultSuppliedLength(), 2, \"registered supplied slots\");\n\n        int256 reportedBackingBefore = accountant.totalBackingSigned();\n        int256 reportedSurplusBefore = accountant.surplus();\n        int256 reportedDistributableBefore = accountant.distributableSurplus();\n\n        int256 correctBackingBefore = int256(DEPOSIT_EVM + SUPPLIED_USDC) - int256(BORROW_USDC);\n        int256 correctSurplusBefore = correctBackingBefore - int256(usdm.totalSupply());\n        int256 correctDistributableBefore = correctSurplusBefore;\n\n        assertEq(reportedBackingBefore, int256(DEPOSIT_EVM + SUPPLIED_USDC), \"reported backing before\");\n        assertEq(correctBackingBefore, int256(DEPOSIT_EVM), \"correct backing before\");\n        assertEq(reportedSurplusBefore, int256(SUPPLIED_USDC), \"reported surplus before\");\n        assertEq(correctSurplusBefore, int256(0), \"correct surplus before\");\n        assertEq(reportedDistributableBefore, int256(SUPPLIED_USDC), \"reported distributable before\");\n        assertEq(correctDistributableBefore, int256(0), \"correct distributable before\");\n        assertGt(reportedDistributableBefore, int256(0), \"current gate sees surplus\");\n        assertEq(correctDistributableBefore, int256(0), \"correct gate sees no surplus\");\n\n        uint256 yieldBefore = usdc.balanceOf(address(yieldEscrow));\n        uint256 vaultBefore = usdc.balanceOf(address(vault));\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 21 hours);\n\n        // Vulnerable path. The Operator uses the normal settle function.\n        // This is not Operator compromise. The accounting failure is that the\n        // Accountant ignores borrow.value while counting supply.value from 0x811.\n        vm.prank(operator);\n        vault.settle(YIELD);\n\n        uint256 yieldAfter = usdc.balanceOf(address(yieldEscrow));\n        uint256 vaultAfter = usdc.balanceOf(address(vault));\n\n        int256 correctBackingAfter = int256(vaultAfter + SUPPLIED_USDC) - int256(BORROW_USDC);\n        int256 correctSurplusAfter = correctBackingAfter - int256(usdm.totalSupply());\n        int256 reportedSurplusAfter = accountant.surplus();\n\n        printReport(\n            borrowL1,\n            suppliedComputed,\n            reportedBackingBefore,\n            correctBackingBefore,\n            reportedSurplusBefore,\n            correctSurplusBefore,\n            reportedDistributableBefore,\n            correctDistributableBefore,\n            yieldBefore,\n            yieldAfter,\n            vaultBefore,\n            vaultAfter,\n            reportedSurplusAfter,\n            correctSurplusAfter\n        );\n\n        assertEq(yieldAfter, YIELD, \"yield escrow funded\");\n        assertEq(yieldAfter - yieldBefore, YIELD, \"yield moved\");\n        assertEq(accountant.totalSettledYield(), YIELD, \"yield settled\");\n        assertEq(vaultAfter, DEPOSIT_EVM - YIELD, \"vault paid real USDC\");\n\n        assertEq(correctBackingAfter, int256(DEPOSIT_EVM - YIELD), \"correct backing after\");\n        assertEq(correctSurplusAfter, -int256(YIELD), \"correct surplus after\");\n\n        assertGt(reportedSurplusAfter, int256(0), \"reported surplus remains positive\");\n        assertLt(correctSurplusAfter, int256(0), \"correct surplus is negative\");\n    }\n\n    function seed(uint256 amount) internal {\n        vm.startPrank(user1);\n        usdc.approve(address(vault), amount);\n        vault.deposit(amount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function openBlp() internal {\n        vm.prank(admin);\n        config.addTradeableAsset(\n            MonetrixConfig.TradeableAsset({\n                perpIndex: ASSET_PERP,\n                spotIndex: ASSET_SPOT,\n                spotPairAssetId: ASSET_PAIR\n            })\n        );\n\n        vm.startPrank(operator);\n        vault.supplyToBlp(uint64(ASSET_SPOT), 1);\n        vault.supplyToBlp(uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX), 1);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function mockAsset() internal {\n        mockToken(ASSET_SPOT, ASSET_WEI_DEC, ASSET_SZ_DEC);\n        mockPerp(ASSET_PERP, ASSET_SZ_DEC);\n        mockPx(ASSET_PERP, ASSET_PX);\n    }\n\n    function mockBlp(uint64 token, uint64 borrowValue, uint64 supplyValue) internal {\n        _PoCMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE)).setResponse(\n            abi.encode(address(vault), token),\n            abi.encode(uint64(0), borrowValue, uint64(0), supplyValue)\n        );\n    }\n\n    function mockToken(uint32 token, uint8 weiDec, uint8 szDec) internal {\n        uint64[] memory spots = new uint64[](0);\n        PrecompileReader.TokenInfo memory info = PrecompileReader.TokenInfo({\n            name: \"MOCK\",\n            spots: spots,\n            deployerTradingFeeShare: 0,\n            deployer: address(0),\n            evmContract: address(0),\n            szDecimals: szDec,\n            weiDecimals: weiDec,\n            evmExtraWeiDecimals: 0\n        });\n\n        _PoCMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_TOKEN_INFO)).setResponse(\n            abi.encode(token),\n            abi.encode(info)\n        );\n    }\n\n    function mockPerp(uint32 perp, uint8 szDec) internal {\n        PrecompileReader.PerpAssetInfo memory info = PrecompileReader.PerpAssetInfo({\n            coin: \"MOCK\",\n            marginTableId: 0,\n            szDecimals: szDec,\n            maxLeverage: 50,\n          